<div class="rt-prose rt-helper-copy">
<div align="justify">
This area presents information to help you in the process of making your payment through the use of a credit card.<br /><br />

<b class="rt-strong rt-tone-cardinal">HOW TO COMPLETE THE PAYMENT</b><br /><br />
You will be required to correctly fill in the details about your card so that the payment can be processed successfully.<br /><br />
<ul>
<li>Expand <strong>Name, Email & Phone</strong> to confirm that the returned details of name, email address and phone number are correct.</li>
<li>Expand <strong>Address, Country & City</strong> to confirm that the details of address, country and city are also correct.</li>
<li>Proceed to enter the details of your card such as your card number, card expiry and the card CVV2 which is located at the back of your card.</li>
<li>Once you are sure that the information is correct, proceed to click on the <button class="btn-xs btn-success"><i class="fas fa-paper-plane"></i> Make Payment </button> button so that the payment can be processed.</li>
<li>When the payment has been confirmed and approved on our side, your product/service will be activated.</li>
</ul><br />
<strong>NOTE:</strong> Should you feel that you have made a mistake or for any other would like to cancel the transaction, you can always <button class="btn-xs default"><i class="fas fa-redo"></i> Reset </button> or <button class="btn-xs default"><i class="fas fa-times"></i> Cancel </button> the respective transaction.

{Msgs::Info('Ensure that you have enough funds including charges on your credit card otherwise the payment may not be completed as expected.')}
<div align="center"><b class="rt-strong">MORE INFORMATION</b></div><br />

The information provided on this page includes invoice details, transaction information, credit card payments among others which are explained in detail below.<br /><br />
<strong>Invoice Details:</strong> This information is specific to the invoice details and includes information such as amount due which is the expected amount to be paid, invoice number that helps to trace the specific invoice, order IP that shows the IP address from which the invoice was generated to mention but a few.<br /><br />
<strong>Transaction Information:</strong> This information is about the transaction that is being made and it includes the order number, transaction ID, payment mode which in this case would be mobile money among others.<br /><br />
<strong>Credit Card Payments:</strong> This is where you will be expected to enter your credit/debit card details as well as some other relevant information.<br /><br />
<strong>NOTE</strong>: It is also possible to open and view the respective invoice should you like to do so by clicking on the invoice number which is given in the invoice details and it will be opened in a new tab.<br  /><br  />

{Msgs::Warning('For more information, please email us on <a rel="mailto:[[CE]]">[[CE]]</a> or call us on <b>[[CP]]</b>')}
</div>
</div>
